##Fire and Smoke Detection using YOLOv12

---

## 📖 Overview

This project presents a **Real-Time Fire and Smoke Detection System** developed using **YOLOv12**, **OpenCV**, and **Python**.

The model is capable of detecting:

* 🔥 Fire
* 🌫️ Smoke

and automatically draws bounding boxes with confidence scores on images and videos.

This system can be used for:

* Forest fire monitoring
* CCTV surveillance
* Industrial safety
* Smart city applications
* Early warning systems

---

## ✨ Features

* ✅ Real-time fire and smoke detection
* ✅ Supports images and videos
* ✅ YOLOv12-based object detection
* ✅ Bounding boxes with confidence scores
* ✅ OpenCV visualization
* ✅ Lightweight and efficient architecture
* ✅ GPU acceleration support

---

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
Fire-Smoke-Detection-YOLOv12
│
├── fire_smoke.py               # Real-time detection script
├── detect_video.py             # Video prediction script
├── fire_smoke_detect.ipynb     # Training notebook
├── best.pt                     # Trained weights
├── requirements.txt
├── README.md
│
├── video_test/
│   ├── forest_fire_test.gif
│   ├── fire-smoke-detect.mp4
│   └── fire_test.mp4
│
└── runs/
    └── detect/
```

---

## 🧠 Model Information

### Model Used

**YOLOv12 Nano (YOLOv12n)**

### Classes

| ID | Class     |
| -- | --------- |
| 0  | 🔥 Fire   |
| 1  | 🌫️ Smoke |

---

## ⚙️ Installation

### Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/Fire-Smoke-Detection-YOLOv12.git

cd Fire-Smoke-Detection-YOLOv12
```

### Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## 📦 Required Libraries

* ultralytics
* opencv-python
* cvzone
* numpy

Install manually:

```bash
pip install ultralytics opencv-python cvzone numpy
```

---

## 🚀 Running Real-Time Detection

Execute:

```bash
python fire_smoke.py
```

This script:

1. Loads the trained YOLOv12 model.
2. Reads frames from the input video.
3. Detects fire and smoke objects.
4. Draws bounding boxes.
5. Displays confidence scores.

---

## 🎥 Video Prediction

Run:

```bash
python detect_video.py
```

Predicted outputs are automatically saved inside:

```text
runs/detect/predict/
```

